# data/history.csv is append-only (new rows only, never reordered). The
# committing workflows rebase-and-retry their push when main advances mid-run
# (see the loops in .github/workflows/*.yml). Across different workflows the
# competing commits touch different files, so those rebases don't conflict — but
# two runs that both append to history.csv (e.g. a manual re-run racing the
# scheduled pull) would collide on the trailing rows. The `union` driver resolves
# that by keeping BOTH sides' lines, which is exactly the append-only semantics
# we want, so the rebase never deadlocks on this file.
data/history.csv merge=union
